A||||4||sqoach||Quick question(s) about water system||||5||
Z||000000||sqoach||06-15-2001||02:56 AM||||When I re-fill my system, burp it and all that, how full should I fill the overflow tank? And after the car's been driven, should the level be the same, or a little higher than it was when filled? Is the system able to suck <I>all</I> the coolant that flowed into the tank back into the system? Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||06-15-2001||11:37 AM||||Fill the coolant overflow tank to the full line, and wait and see if it sucks in any coolant. I alway continue to keep the tank near full right after burping the system. Chances are it will puke it up once you shut the car off, but it will ensure no air bubbles are sucked into the cooling system. The point of the overflow tank is really so air can excape from the system, by letting it go under water, the coolant is sucked in to replace it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||06-17-2001||06:46 PM||||Well what about the level? Should it go up any after you fill it? Mine seems to go up a bit after I've driven it, and never goes back down to where it was. Just stays at that higher level.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||06-18-2001||04:11 PM||||???||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-18-2001||07:42 PM||||AS I remember... there is a full mark on the fan side of the recovery tank. It should be up near that mark when the system is hot.||||reg||1
